// The rune spine, as a golden-C witness.
//
// A standalone write-rune plus its `.write` stores.  The `selfhost-rune` gate
// asserts the emitted C carries the `volatile <T> *` binding (presence) AND
// that each `.write` lowers to EXACTLY ONE volatile store (multiplicity) —
// both directions of it, since elision and duplication are distinct betrayals.
//
// The address is a real custom-chip register (COP1LC, $DFF080), so this compiles
// under `cc -ansi -pedantic -Wall` but is NOT run on the host: a store to
// $DFF080 moves no copper here.  ram_roundtrip.exl is the runnable witness.

fn main() {
    rune cop1lc: u32 at 0xDFF080 write;
    cop1lc.write(0x12345);
    cop1lc.write(0);
}
